+# The 3D auras (Orb's direction, 2026-10-18)
+
+Owner: VFX Director. Built in scratch and parked (`docs/vfx/pending/aura3d/`), **off by default**. Orb's words (homework, 2026-10-18): "cool, pulsating, 3D visual auras that can shimmer, froth, undulate etc. based on whose aura. Ideally protagonist and rival have similar but inverted themes on their auras, not just color ... develop a unique aura style to convey each character's power foundation." Not a clearance; **Legal has not seen it** (see the last section).
+
+## The idea
+
+One shell round each fighter, a real 3D mesh seen from the side camera, its surface drawn in object space so the pattern wraps round the body and drifts like a volume (the fighter's own body hides the shell's far half). The Protagonist's and the Anti-hero's are the **same structure with every axis inverted**, each built on that fighter's power foundation (Narrative's voice bibles: the Protagonist's blood runs "warm to boiling, and it costs him", the Anti-hero's "pride outranks his justice" and he "swallows that pride only when he has to"):
+
+| | **Protagonist: the boil** (a furnace giving heat away) | **Anti-hero: the facets** (cold pride, held in) |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| Shell | larger (x1.08): spent outward | smaller (x0.9): held in tight |
+| Pulse | swells outward and relaxes, an exhale (fast out, slow back), 0.9 Hz, 10% | draws inward and holds, a smooth inhale, 0.5 Hz, 6% |
+| Skin | round **bubbles** that grow, ring and thin out, and a finer froth between them that thickens with the tier: bright RINGS on a clear skin | a lattice of crystal **facets**: bright CELLS between dark SEAMS (the boil's polarity flipped); at tier 3 and up the seams are lit from inside (pride cracking) |
+| Drift | the skin rises up the shell like convection; each pulse sends a bright band UP | the skin settles down the shell like cold air; each pulse sends a band DOWN |
+| Shimmer | irregular, restless (bubble lives 1.8 s, hashed) | ordered and still: each facet glints in its own slow turn (0.14 Hz), like frost |
+| Edge | soft rim, the surface undulates (3D noise along the normal, 12%) | crisp rim, smooth crystal (3%) |
+| Colour | the lane colour (azure) with a lighter tint | the lane colour (orchid) with a lighter tint and a dark shade for the seams |
+
+`effects_check` holds the inversion: all eight axes (shape, pulse direction, drift, size, restlessness, rim, undulation, froth) differ in the stated direction. Any other fighter takes a `default` theme (a milder boil) until its own foundation is written.
+
+## Files (all VFX's)
+
+New: `render/vfx/aura3d.gd` (`VfxAura3D`: the themes, the pure `params()` that gives every uniform, the colours, the rate bound), `aura3d_view.gd` (`VfxAura3DView`: a `SphereMesh` shell per fighter, placed round his body, a child of the trail view), `shaders/aura3d.gdshader`, `data/vfx/aura3d.json`, `tools/schemas/vfx-aura3d.schema.json`, this page. Changed: `vfx_hub.gd` (`aura3d_enabled`, `aura3d_demo`, `set_aura3d()`; the standing aura's eased level also runs when the 3D aura is on), `trail_view.gd` (the child), `tools/schemas/map.json`, `render/core/warmup.gd` (one line), `effects_check.gd` (`_aura3d`, 10 check lines), `docs/vfx/README.md`. `transform_view.gd` and `vfx_layer.gd` are untouched.
+
+**To turn it on:** `hub.set_aura3d(true)` (it switches the old flat standing aura off, so there is one aura, not two; `false` puts it back). It then shows on the standing aura's own rules (while a fighter charges, attacks, rushes or fires, eased in over 8 ticks, held 18, out over 24, never while hidden, down, launched or in a transformation), at the fighter's tier. `hub.aura3d_demo = true` shows both at full level whatever they are doing (the capture, the prototype).
+
+## The rules it keeps, and measured
+
+- **Colour:** the lane colour (`VfxAura.lane_color`, which already swaps a fire colour or white for the Anti-hero's accent), a lighter tint (saturation floor 0.3, value ceiling 0.93: never white) and a dark shade; the largest R/(R+G+B) of any of them for the two lane colours, a fire colour and white as inputs is 0.35 (checked, stored and linear). Alpha-blended, never additive, so overlaps cannot add up to white. Drawn alpha capped at 0.5.
+- **Rates:** every rate at most 0.9 Hz (the cap is 2); the calm form (Reduce flashing, the game's default, or Reduced motion) pulses smaller and slower (x0.4, x0.6), the froth and the band turn at half speed, the bubbles hold at full size and nothing pops; the facets glint at half speed.
+- **No flame shape streaming upward, no lightning, no spiky silhouette**; it never appears at rest (the standing aura's own rule); the stacking rule (no crouch and scream with it) is the director's.
+- **Flash clips** of the showcase (both fighters standing at full level on the plains, the tier rising every 5 s, 1,250 ticks, the official analyser): **both modes PASS with 0 flashes on every reading, red 0.**
+- **Collapse, both modes, with the code in and inert (the switch off):** PASS, normal 2 / 2.5 / 1, reduced 2 / 2 / 0.5 (primary / area-15% / memory), red 0.
+- Native checks: `effects_check` `_aura3d` (data = defaults; the eight inversions; rates; alpha cap; colours; params pure, the tier grows the shell, the Protagonist's is larger; the calm form; clamps; off by default and the old aura's return; the view builds hidden).
+- **No timing taken** (the machine is shared): two shells a pane, one 64 by 32 sphere each, a 27-cell cellular search twice a fragment (the froth) on the Protagonist's; the fill is the size of a fighter. Counts and an estimate, not a measurement; Performance's bench is owed before it is on by default.
+
+## Limits, and what is not done
+
+- **It is a prototype for Orb's eye.** The GIFs in `homework/auras-in-motion/` (private) are a standing pair on the plains; it has not been seen on a moving fighter in a brawl, in the city, at night, or beside beams. The shell is a half dome where it meets the ground (the ground hides its lower half).
+- **Not built:** per-tier names for the transformations, a hit-reaction (the shell flinching), the last stand's ring (aura.gd's mark is left alone), the Empress's and the Cyborg's themes (a `default` takes them; their foundations are Narrative's to supply), the beam's own aura link.
+- **Legal:** the standing aura's rule (`docs/legal/rule-of-cool-screen.md`) asks for "a thin outline or rings in the fighter's lane colour, not a flame shape streaming upward, no gold, white or red, no lightning, no spiky hair". This is a richer surface (a shell with froth and facets), still a lane-colour shell with no flame, lightning or spikes, but **it is not a thin outline and the earlier screen's re-screen of the aura "when VFX's first version exists" is now due.** It stays off until Legal rules.
+- **Needs from others:** Legal (the re-screen); Narrative (a power foundation for the Empress and the Cyborg, one sentence each); Art (the tint and the seam shade against the lane colours); Tools (fixtures for `vfx-aura3d.schema.json`: one valid and three invalid, e.g. a `pulse_hz` of 2.5, an `alpha_max` of 0.6, a `froth` entry of 1.5).
+
+## An inverted hull on the fighter's own mesh: the energy follows his real silhouette (2026-10-22; supersedes the shell above)
+
+The look gate sent the shell and the rim band back (ADR 0010): a thin ellipse round each fighter is not his outline and not the living aura Orb described. The aura is now a **second outline pass on the fighter's own skinned mesh**. The body already has an outline (`fighter_hull.gdshader`: back faces only, every vertex pushed along the direction baked into its NORMAL by its reach in UV2.x). The aura (`shaders/aura3d.gdshader`) is chained after it and pushes the same vertices a further `hull_bh` of the body's height (6.5 to 12 percent by tier, in model units, so as thick on a small fighter as on a big one), so it stands off the real silhouette in every pose, limb by limb, and the body's front faces hide the rest through the depth test. Three things keep the body clear (the EP's look gate of 2026-10-22: no stroke inside the body's outline, even with a hand over the torso):
+- **the depth test against the opaque scene (`hull_gap`, 60 units):** a hull face lying over the torso (an arm's, the head's) has the body just behind it, while the fringe outside the silhouette has the ground or the sky far behind; the fragment reads the opaque depth behind it (`hint_depth_texture`) and is discarded unless the scene is at least `hull_gap` units farther than itself. This is what removes the strokes over the torso, the arm and the other fighter;
+- only the silhouette's fringe is kept: the back faces that remain turn away from the camera, so the fragment keeps the grazing ones (`fringe_lo` 0.22 to `fringe_hi` 0.5 of facing);
+- the band is thin, a constant distance off the body (7 percent of his height at every tier), ragged only a little at the edge, and alpha-blended at most 0.5.
+
+## Legal's conditions (fx06, docs/legal/aura3d-screen.md)
+1. **Transient, one mark, never a standing glow:** the aura runs as a BURST (aura.gd `burst`): when a fighter starts charging or attacking (the standing aura's rising edge) and the last burst ended at least `burst_gap` (240 ticks, four seconds) ago, it rises over 18 ticks, holds for 54 (0.9 s), falls over 48, and is gone whatever he is doing, until a new start after the gap. It does not grow with the tier (the same distance off the body at every tier). With the 3D aura on, the old flat standing aura is off.
+2. **No tongues, crackle, pulse of the whole aura, or white/gold/red core:** the band's thickness and alpha no longer breathe with the pulse (the pulse now only sends the travelling band along the body); the edge noise is a few percent of the band; the tier-3 lit seams are inside the facets, not strokes between the fighter and the ground.
+3. **Rates and alpha asserted:** pulse, shimmer and froth at most 2 Hz (held under 1), `alpha_max` 0.5; the closed schema rejects 2.5 Hz and 0.6 alpha; proposed fixtures for Tools are in `fixtures.json` beside this page.
+4. **Calm form** (Reduce flashing): slower, lower alpha, as before. **5. Faces and glasses:** nothing is drawn inside the outline, so no stroke can cover a face or the glasses. **6. Not in public material** until Orb approves the look.
+
+## The water, the old laptop, the registry
+The hull is drawn before the water (render priority -1), so a fighter below the waterline gets his band under the water's tint as his body has it. It is chained after the outline pass only while its level is up (FighterView), so it costs nothing when the aura is off. The per-fighter hull materials are pruned to the current fighters at each match's reset.
+
+Inside the band the surface is alive in object space, so it wraps and moves with the limbs: **the Protagonist's boil** (the band swells out and relaxes, bubbles grow, ring and thin out, froth between them thickening with the tier, the skin drifting up, a bright band up the body each pulse, a ragged breathing edge) and **the Anti-hero's facets** (the band draws in and holds, hard dark seams between bright crystal cells glinting in turn, settling down, a band down the body each pulse, a smooth edge, the seams lit from inside from tier 3). Every inversion of the first cut is kept; the rates, the lane colours (never gold, white or red) and the alpha cap are unchanged.
+
+How it is wired: `VfxAura3D.hull_material(fighter)` makes one hull material per fighter; Rendering's FighterView chains it after the outline pass and gives it the projection anchor each frame (a few lines, a grant: `grant-fighter-view.patch`); the view (`aura3d_view.gd`) only writes its parameters each frame from the standing aura's level, so it works the same in every pane. Behind the same switch as before (`hub.aura3d_enabled`, off; turning it on turns the old flat standing aura off). Not a Legal clearance: Legal's earlier rule asked for a thin outline; this is richer and needs their re-screen.
+
+Limits: the fringe test is a screen-space heuristic of the baked normals, so a hand crossing the torso can still tint a little of the body; the band is not a perfect offset of the sprite (it is the mesh's, so it stands off by model units, a little more where the baked normals are long); the headless outline check needs a window and was not run.
+
+## The first draw (Performance, 2026-10-22)
+A hitch of 50 to 110 ms at the first tick the aura draws appeared although the shader is in the boot warm-up's table: the pipeline is the shader on the SKINNED fighter mesh with the depth read, in the REAL pane's viewport (the driver sets pipelines up per viewport, so the warm-up's own 64 pixel viewport did not warm it). `VfxAura3D.warm_node()` is a real fighter body (AnimBody as FighterView builds it) with a hull chained after its outline, which VFX's `warm.gd` hands to the boot warm-up (park `warm-first-use`) to stand in the pane's view for its three frames behind the notice. Measured on Performance's cold repro (the city beam scene with the aura held up): the tick-6 hitch (75 to 111 ms) is gone.
